            {
                "list": {
                    "items": [
                        "The US Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) allows unused prescription drugs to be mailed back to pharmacies or other approved sites. Packages for mailing are made available at pharmacies or other drug disposal sites. Contact your local pharmacy before mailing unused drugs.",
                        "You can find more details about drug take-back options at [<a href='https://www.deatakeback.com/'><u>deatakeback.com/</u></a>].",
                        "To find more take-back sites near you, visit [<a href='apps2.deadiversion.usdoj.gov/pubdispsearch/spring/main?execution=e2s1/'><u>apps2.deadiversion.usdoj.gov/pubdispsearch/spring/main?execution=e2s1</u></a>]."
                    ],
                    "items_replacements": {
                        "default": {
                            "Spanish": [
                                "La Administraci\u00f3n para el Control de Drogas de Estados Unidos (DEA, por su nombre en ingl\u00e9s) permite que los f\u00e1rmacos prescritos no utilizados se env\u00eden de vuelta por correo postal a farmacias o a otros sitios aprobados. Los paquetes para enviar por correo postal est\u00e1n disponibles en farmacias u otros sitios de eliminaci\u00f3n de f\u00e1rmacos. Comun\u00edquese con su farmacia local antes de enviar f\u00e1rmacos no utilizados por correo postal.",
                                "Puede encontrar m\u00e1s detalles sobre las opciones de devoluci\u00f3n de f\u00e1rmacos en [<a href='https://www.deatakeback.com/'><u>deatakeback.com/</u></a>].",
                                "Para encontrar m\u00e1s sitios de devoluci\u00f3n de f\u00e1rmacos cerca de usted, visite [<a href='apps2.deadiversion.usdoj.gov/pubdispsearch/spring/main?execution=e2s1/'><u>apps2.deadiversion.usdoj.gov/pubdispsearch/spring/main?execution=e2s1</u></a>]."
                            ]
                        }
                    },
                    "list_attributes": {
                        "bulletFontSize": 5.0,
                        "bulletOffsetY": -5.0,
                        "bulletType": "bullet",
                        "start": "\u25aa"
                    },
                    "list_item_attributes": {
                        "spaceAfter": 5.0,
                        "spaceBefore": 2.0
                    },
                    "text_style": {
                        "fontSize": 12.0,
                        "parent_style": "ParagraphText"
                    }
                }
            },
            {
                "paragraph": {
                    "string": "<b><u>Other Ways to Dispose of Medications:</u></b>",
                    "string_replacements": {
                        "default": {
                            "Spanish": "<b><u>Otras Maneras de Desechar los Medicamentos:</u></b>"
                        }
                    },
                    "text_style": {
                        "parent_style": "ParagraphText"
                    }
                }
            },
            {
                "list": {
                    "items": [
                        "Remove the drugs from their original containers. Mix them with something undesirable, such as used coffee grounds, dirt, or cat litter.",
                        "Put the mixture in something you can close, such as a zip-lock bag, to stop it from spilling out. Then throw away the container.",
                        "Some prescription medications may be safely flushed. For a list of what can be flushed, please visit [<a href='fda.gov/drugs/disposal-unused-medicines-what-you-should-know/drug-disposal-fdas-flush-list-certain-medicines'><u>fda.gov/drugs/disposal-unused-medicines-what-you-should-know/drug-disposal-fdas-flush-list-certain-medicines</u></a>].",
                        "If you have any questions about your medications, ask your doctor or pharmacist.",
                        "For more details on the safe disposal of drugs, please contact your local pharmacy or police department. You can also visit [<a href= 'hhs.gov/opioids/prevention/safely-dispose-drugs/index.html'><u>hhs.gov/opioids/prevention/safely-dispose-drugs/index.html</u></a>]."
                    ],
                    "items_replacements": {
                        "default": {
                            "Spanish": [
                                "Retire los f\u00e1rmacos de sus contenedores originales. M\u00e9zclelos con algo indeseable, como posos de caf\u00e9 usados, tierra o arena para gatos.",
                                "Coloque la mezcla en algo que pueda cerrar, como una bolsa con cierre herm\u00e9tico, para evitar que se derrame. A continuaci\u00f3n, deseche el contenedor.",
                                "Algunos medicamentos prescritos se pueden desechar de manera segura por el inodoro. Para obtener una lista de lo que se puede desechar por el inodoro, visite [<a href='fda.gov/drugs/disposal-unused-medicines-what-you-should-know/drug-disposal-fdas-flush-list-certain-medicines'><u>fda.gov/drugs/disposal-unused-medicines-what-you-should-know/drug-disposal-fdas-flush-list-certain-medicines</u></a>].",
                                "Si tiene alguna pregunta sobre sus medicamentos, consulte a su doctor o farmac\u00e9utico.",
                                "Para obtener m\u00e1s detalles sobre la eliminaci\u00f3n segura de los f\u00e1rmacos, comun\u00edquese con su farmacia local o con el departamento de polic\u00eda. Tambi\u00e9n puede visitar [<a href= 'hhs.gov/opioids/prevention/safely-dispose-drugs/index.html'><u>hhs.gov/opioids/prevention/safely-dispose-drugs/index.html</u></a>]."
                            ]
                        }
                    },
